From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:22:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sf: e-ink: fixes from an audit: holds, one-shots, damage, no
 pass at eink_enhance=0

- A settle one-shot cleared up to 500 ms later no longer removes a sleep, wake,
  unlock or page hold's own one-shot (the sleep screen's GC16 was lost).
- A held page turn released after another app changed the mode shows that mode;
  it no longer writes the reader's menu mode or page mode over it.
- The fingerprint check reads the time after the property, not before an IPC.
- Page holds only for changes of at least min_area_pct (a cursor or progress
  line within 2 s of a tap came out as a GC16 page); the touch cadence only
  extends FAST for frames with damage.
- Unlocking into a reader's full-screen page puts the page mode back and shows
  the page with its GC16 at the release, not the wake mode and a second hold.
- Going to sleep during a wake or unlock hold keeps the page mode under the
  reader's menu mode; a sleep mode equal to the fast mode still restores the
  user's mode; eink_sleep=0 while asleep clears an armed one-shot.
- Damage share against the panel's area, only the panel's layers (a parallax
  wallpaper made home screen changes look 2-4x smaller; virtual displays).
- debug.sf.eink_enhance=0 with the render pass is no pass at all (it ran the
  enhancement pass's contrast clip); the damage padding is bounded.

- The developer option "Disable HW overlays" can no longer switch off the
  forced GPU composition that debug.sf.force_client_composition asks for.
---
 .../CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp          |  9 ++-
 .../DisplayHardware/EinkMotion.cpp            | 67 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../DisplayHardware/EinkMotion.h              |  3 +-
 services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp    | 25 ++++++-
 4 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
index 48a361c..5b63106 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
@@ -1835,6 +1835,11 @@ EinkEnhance getEinkEnhance(bool trackKernelDither) {
         c.crush = t.crush;
         c.black = 0.f;
         c.white = 1.f;
+    } else if (c.render >= 3) {
+        // debug.sf.eink_enhance=0 with the render pass: no pass at all (the bench's raw
+        // profiles). It fell through to the enhancement pass's branch below, whose contrast from
+        // HiBreakParts (48..208) alone turned the pass on and clipped every grey.
+        c.render = 0;
     } else {
         c.render = 0;
         const bool blackAndWhite = mode == 0 || mode == 0xb2 || mode == 0xb3 || mode == 0x02 ||
@@ -1876,7 +1881,9 @@ int32_t einkDamagePadding(const EinkEnhance& e) {
     } else if (e.strength > 0.f) {
         reach = 2.f * e.radius;
     }
-    return reach > 0.f ? static_cast<int32_t>(std::ceil(reach)) + 1 : 0;
+    // Bounded: the radius comes from a property, and the padded rectangle must not overflow.
+    return reach > 0.f ? std::min(64, static_cast<int32_t>(std::ceil(std::min(reach, 63.f))) + 1)
+                       : 0;
 }
 
 } // namespace
